{
  "id": "RAW_92062bf5ea",
  "title": "认识 Thinking Machines Inkling 2 Mini：可在 32GB Mac 上运行的 26B 循环式 MoE",
  "url": "https://www.marktechpost.com/2026/11/21/thinking-machines-inkling-2-mini-looped-transformer/",
  "date": "2026-11-21 20:13:52",
  "author": "Asif Razzaq",
  "siteName": "MarkTechPost",
  "content": "<html>\n <head></head>\n <body>\n  <div class=\"td-a-rec td-a-rec-id-content_top  tdi_77 td_block_template_1\">\n   <!-- MTP Preferred Source badge : DESKTOP (plain link, no script; hidden below 640px) -->\n   <div id=\"mtp-pref-desk\">\n    <a class=\"mtp-pref-btn\" href=\"https://www.google.com/preferences/source?q=marktechpost.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" aria-label=\"Add Marktechpost as a preferred source on Google\"><img src=\"https://www.gstatic.com/images/branding/googleg/1x/googleg_standard_color_128dp.png\" alt=\"\"><span class=\"mtp-pref-txt\"><span style=\"display:block!important\">Add as a preferred</span><span style=\"display:block!important\">source on Google</span></span></a>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://thinkingmachines.ai/news/inkling-2-mini/\">Thinking Machines Lab</a> has released <strong>Inkling 2 Mini</strong>, an open-weight looped transformer with 26.4B total parameters. The model reuses its middle layers 3 times per token instead of adding more weights. That keeps the checkpoint near 20GB, small enough for a 32GB Mac or 1 NVIDIA DGX Spark. For developers, Inkling 2 Mini is a local option for agentic coding, tool use and document work. It ships under <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Mini\">Apache 2.0 on Hugging Face</a>, with hosted inference and fine-tuning on <a href=\"https://tinker.thinkingmachines.ai/playground\">Tinker</a>.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-tl-dr\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>TL;DR</strong></h2>\n  <ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n   <li><strong>Size:</strong> 26.4B total, 3.4B active (5.4B effective per token with looping), up to 1M-token context.</li>\n   <li><strong>Runs on:</strong> Apple silicon with 32GB+ memory, 1 NVIDIA DGX Spark, or GPUs with 32GB+ VRAM. GGUF builds via Unsloth and llama.cpp.</li>\n   <li><strong>Performance:</strong> 20.1 on the Artificial Analysis Index, tied with Qwen3.8-27B (self-reported).</li>\n   <li><strong>Best:</strong> 79.2% on SWE-bench Verified (bash only).</li>\n   <li><strong>Worst:</strong> 15.2% on HLE-Diamond and 50.0% on MultiChallenge.</li>\n   <li><strong>Bottom line:</strong> Best: strong agentic coding from a 20GB checkpoint. Worst: weaker knowledge recall and multi-turn instruction following.</li>\n  </ul>\n  <h2 id=\"h-what-is-inkling-2-mini\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>What is Inkling 2 Mini?</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Inkling 2 Mini is a sparse Mixture-of-Experts model from Thinking Machines that loops its middle layers. It accepts text and images and returns text only.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It follows Inkling 2 Small, a 594B-parameter model released on November 5.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-how-does-the-looped-transformer-work\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How does the looped transformer work?</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The model stores 24 layers, grouped into 4 blocks of 6. The first and last blocks run once. The 2 middle blocks run 3 times with shared weights. That gives 48 layer applications per token from 24 layers of weights.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Each pass after the first receives a “message” from the previous pass. Thinking Machines carries it with <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.15031\">Attention Residuals</a> and a learned gate. Feed-forward layers use 128 experts, with 8 routed per token.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Looping the middle layers gave a 1.51x to 1.91x compute-equivalent gain. Looping the last layers gave only 1.24x to 1.36x. The middle-loop variant won 27 of 28 evaluations.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Looping costs training compute but saves inference. An unlooped baseline used 7.5% less training compute. It needed 140% more inference compute to match the looped model’s loss on 512k-token agentic traces.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-how-was-inkling-2-mini-trained\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How was Inkling 2 Mini trained?</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Training began with 384 experts per layer, with 8 active per token. At midtraining, the team pruned two-thirds of them and kept the 128 most-used experts. A 1T-token distillation run from a larger internal Inkling model then healed the pruned model. Post-training used SFT, then RL over 2.2T tokens and 2,000 steps, plus on-policy distillation.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Expert layers are trained and deployed in NVFP4. The last 4 layers use MXFP8. Thinking Machines says this removes quantization conversion loss. A research variant, <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/thinkingmachines/TML-d24-varloop-research\">TML-d24-varloop-research</a>, trains with 1 to 5 passes.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-how-does-inkling-2-mini-perform-on-benchmarks\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How does Inkling 2 Mini perform on benchmarks?</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">All Inkling scores below are self-reported by Thinking Machines. Coding is the strongest area. Inkling 2 Mini scores 79.2% on SWE-bench Verified (bash only) and 77.9% on SWE-bench Pro v2 (Hard). It reaches 48.2% on DeepSWE v1.1, where <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B\">Qwen’s own card</a> lists Qwen3.8-27B at 42.2%. On Terminal Bench v2.1 it scores 71.6%, behind Qwen3.8-27B at 73.0%.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Agentic search also holds up: 79.0% on BrowseComp with compaction and 82.7% on MCP Atlas. For documents and vision, it posts 92.8% on OmniDocBench v1.6 and 74.9% on MMMU Pro. On reasoning, it scores 86.6% on GPQA Diamond and 49.3% on ARC-AGI-2.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Efficiency is the headline claim. On Stanford’s Intelligence per Watt metric, Thinking Machines reports 0.703 on a DGX Spark. It lists Qwen3.6-35B-A3B at 0.430 and Gemma-4-26B-A4B at 0.159.</p>\n  <div id=\"mtp-ink2m-wrap\" style=\"margin:24px auto;\">\n   <iframe class=\"lazyload\" id=\"mtp-ink2m-frame\" title=\"Inkling 2 Mini interactive explainer\" loading=\"lazy\" scrolling=\"no\" srcdoc=\"&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html lang=&quot;en&quot;&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta charset=&quot;utf-8&quot;&gt;&lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width,initial-scale=1&quot;&gt;\n&lt;title&gt;Inkling 2 Mini explainer&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;style&gt;\nhtml,body{margin:0!important;padding:0!important;background:transparent!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m{--ink:#111111;--paper:#f7f6f2;--card:#ffffff;--mute:#6f6e69;--line:#dcdad3;--soft:#ecebe5;--warn:#9a3b1e;--mtp:#76B900;\nfont-family:&quot;Inter&quot;,system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,sans-serif!important;color:var(--ink)!important;background:var(--paper)!important;\nmax-width:880px;margin:0 auto;border:1px solid var(--line)!important;border-radius:14px;padding:22px 22px 14px;box-sizing:border-box;}\n#mtp-ink2m *{box-sizing:border-box;}\n#mtp-ink2m hr,#mtp-ink2m p:empty,#mtp-ink2m del,#mtp-ink2m s{display:none!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .hd{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-end;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:14px;}\n#mtp-ink2m .kicker{font:600 11px/1 &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;,ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace!important;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--mute)!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m h3{margin:6px 0 0!important;font-size:24px!important;line-height:1.15!important;font-weight:800!important;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:var(--ink)!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .pill{font:600 11px &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;,ui-monospace,monospace;border:1px solid var(--ink)!important;border-radius:99px;padding:5px 10px;background:var(--card)!important;color:var(--ink)!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .tabs{display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)!important;padding-bottom:10px;margin-bottom:16px;}\n#mtp-ink2m .tab{appearance:none;cursor:pointer;font:600 13px &quot;Inter&quot;,system-ui,sans-serif;padding:8px 13px;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid var(--line)!important;background:var(--card)!important;color:var(--ink)!important;transition:all .2s;}\n#mtp-ink2m .tab:hover{border-color:var(--ink)!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .tab.on{background:var(--ink)!important;color:var(--paper)!important;border-color:var(--ink)!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .panel{display:none;animation:mtpInkFade .35s ease;}\n#mtp-ink2m .panel.on{display:block;}\n@keyframes mtpInkFade{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(6px)}to{opacity:1;transform:none}}\n#mtp-ink2m .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:10px;}\n#mtp-ink2m .tile{background:var(--card)!important;border:1px solid var(--line)!important;border-radius:10px;padding:14px;cursor:pointer;transition:transform .2s,border-color .2s;}\n#mtp-ink2m .tile:hover{transform:translateY(-2px);border-color:var(--ink)!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .tile .v{font-size:26px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.02em;}\n#mtp-ink2m .tile .l{font:600 11px &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;,ui-monospace,monospace;color:var(--mute)!important;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;margin-top:2px;}\n#mtp-ink2m .tile .x{font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.45;color:var(--mute)!important;max-height:0;overflow:hidden;transition:max-height .3s,margin .3s;}\n#mtp-ink2m .tile.open .x{max-height:90px;margin-top:8px;}\n#mtp-ink2m .note{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--mute)!important;margin:12px 0 0;line-height:1.5;}\n#mtp-ink2m .loop{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;justify-content:center;margin:8px 0 6px;flex-wrap:wrap;}\n#mtp-ink2m .blk{width:120px;height:86px;border:2px solid var(--line)!important;border-radius:10px;background:var(--card)!important;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;transition:all .35s;position:relative;}\n#mtp-ink2m .blk b{font-size:14px;}\n#mtp-ink2m .blk span{font:500 11px &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;,monospace;color:var(--mute)!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .blk.act{border-color:var(--ink)!important;background:var(--ink)!important;color:var(--paper)!important;transform:scale(1.05);}\n#mtp-ink2m .blk.act span{color:#cfcdc6!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .mid{position:relative;display:flex;gap:8px;padding:10px;border:1.5px dashed var(--mute)!important;border-radius:12px;}\n#mtp-ink2m .mid .tag{position:absolute;top:-10px;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);background:var(--paper)!important;padding:0 8px;font:600 10.5px &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;,monospace;color:var(--mute)!important;white-space:nowrap;}\n#mtp-ink2m .arr{font-size:18px;color:var(--mute)!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .ctrl{display:flex;gap:8px;justify-content:center;margin:14px 0 6px;flex-wrap:wrap;}\n#mtp-ink2m .btn{cursor:pointer;font:600 13px &quot;Inter&quot;,sans-serif;padding:8px 14px;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid var(--ink)!important;background:var(--card)!important;color:var(--ink)!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .btn.pri{background:var(--ink)!important;color:var(--paper)!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .counter{text-align:center;font:600 13px &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;,monospace;margin-top:6px;}\n#mtp-ink2m .counter big{font-size:30px;font-family:&quot;Inter&quot;,sans-serif;font-weight:800;}\n#mtp-ink2m .meter{height:8px;background:var(--soft)!important;border-radius:99px;overflow:hidden;margin:8px auto 0;max-width:420px;}\n#mtp-ink2m .meter i{display:block;height:100%;width:0;background:var(--ink)!important;transition:width .45s;}\n#mtp-ink2m .msg{text-align:center;font-size:13px;color:var(--mute)!important;min-height:20px;margin-top:8px;}\n#mtp-ink2m .cats{display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:12px;}\n#mtp-ink2m .cat{cursor:pointer;font:600 12px &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;,monospace;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:99px;border:1px solid var(--line)!important;background:var(--card)!important;color:var(--ink)!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .cat.on{border-color:var(--ink)!important;background:var(--ink)!important;color:var(--paper)!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:190px 1fr 62px;gap:10px;align-items:center;margin:7px 0;font-size:13px;}\n#mtp-ink2m .row .n{font-weight:600;}\n#mtp-ink2m .row .n small{display:block;font-weight:500;color:var(--mute)!important;font-size:11px;}\n#mtp-ink2m .bar{height:16px;background:var(--soft)!important;border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden;}\n#mtp-ink2m .bar i{display:block;height:100%;width:0;border-radius:4px;transition:width .8s cubic-bezier(.2,.8,.2,1);background:var(--ink)!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .bar.c i{background:#a9a79f!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .bar.w i{background:var(--warn)!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .row .s{font:700 13px &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;,monospace;text-align:right;}\n#mtp-ink2m .mems{display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;}\n#mtp-ink2m .verdict{margin-top:14px;padding:14px;border-radius:10px;border:1px solid var(--line)!important;background:var(--card)!important;font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;min-height:70px;}\n#mtp-ink2m .verdict b.ok{color:#1f6b2a!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .verdict b.no{color:var(--warn)!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m pre,#mtp-ink2m code{font:12.5px/1.5 &quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;,ui-monospace,monospace!important;background:#111!important;color:#f7f6f2!important;border:0!important;border-radius:8px;}\n#mtp-ink2m pre{padding:10px 12px;margin:10px 0 0;overflow-x:auto;white-space:pre;}\n#mtp-ink2m .two{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;}\n#mtp-ink2m .two .box{background:var(--card)!important;border:1px solid var(--line)!important;border-radius:10px;padding:14px;}\n#mtp-ink2m .two h4{margin:0 0 8px!important;font-size:13px!important;font-family:&quot;JetBrains Mono&quot;,monospace!important;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--ink)!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .two ul{margin:0;padding-left:18px;font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.55;}\n#mtp-ink2m .ft{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:16px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)!important;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--mute)!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .ft a{color:var(--mute)!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .ft .brand{color:var(--mtp)!important;font-weight:700;}\n@media (max-width:640px){\n#mtp-ink2m{padding:16px 14px 10px;}\n#mtp-ink2m h3{font-size:20px!important;}\n#mtp-ink2m .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;}\n#mtp-ink2m .blk{width:84px;height:72px;}\n#mtp-ink2m .blk b{font-size:12px;}\n#mtp-ink2m .row{grid-template-columns:120px 1fr 52px;font-size:12px;}\n#mtp-ink2m .two{grid-template-columns:1fr;}\n#mtp-ink2m .arr{display:none;}\n}\n&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body&gt;\n&lt;div id=&quot;mtp-ink2m&quot;&gt;\n &lt;div class=&quot;hd&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;kicker&quot;&gt;Thinking Machines · Nov 20, 2026&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Inkling 2 Mini, explained&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;pill&quot;&gt;Looped MoE · Apache 2.0&lt;/div&gt;\n &lt;/div&gt;\n &lt;div class=&quot;tabs&quot; role=&quot;tablist&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;button class=&quot;tab on&quot; data-p=&quot;ov&quot;&gt;Overview&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button class=&quot;tab&quot; data-p=&quot;lp&quot;&gt;The loop&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button class=&quot;tab&quot; data-p=&quot;bm&quot;&gt;Benchmarks&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button class=&quot;tab&quot; data-p=&quot;ef&quot;&gt;Efficiency&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button class=&quot;tab&quot; data-p=&quot;run&quot;&gt;Can I run it?&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;button class=&quot;tab&quot; data-p=&quot;tr&quot;&gt;Trade-offs&lt;/button&gt;\n &lt;/div&gt;\n\n &lt;div class=&quot;panel on&quot; id=&quot;p-ov&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;grid&quot;&gt;\n   &lt;div class=&quot;tile&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;v&quot;&gt;26.4B&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;l&quot;&gt;Total params&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;x&quot;&gt;Stored weights. Knowledge mostly scales with this number, per Thinking Machines.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n   &lt;div class=&quot;tile&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;v&quot;&gt;3.4B&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;l&quot;&gt;Active params&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;x&quot;&gt;5.4B effective per token, because the middle layers run 3 times.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n   &lt;div class=&quot;tile&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;v&quot;&gt;48&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;l&quot;&gt;Layer passes / token&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;x&quot;&gt;24 stored layers. The middle 12 run 3 times with shared weights.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n   &lt;div class=&quot;tile&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;v&quot;&gt;1M&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;l&quot;&gt;Context (tokens)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;x&quot;&gt;Up to 1M tokens. Input: text and images. Output: text only.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n   &lt;div class=&quot;tile&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;v&quot;&gt;~20GB&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;l&quot;&gt;Checkpoint&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;x&quot;&gt;NVFP4 expert layers, MXFP8 last 4 layers. Single Safetensors checkpoint.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n   &lt;div class=&quot;tile&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;v&quot;&gt;128 / 8&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;l&quot;&gt;Experts / routed&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;x&quot;&gt;Pruned from 384 experts at midtraining, then healed with 1T distilled tokens.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;p class=&quot;note&quot;&gt;Tap any tile for detail. All figures from the Thinking Machines blog and model card.&lt;/p&gt;\n &lt;/div&gt;\n\n &lt;div class=&quot;panel&quot; id=&quot;p-lp&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;loop&quot;&gt;\n   &lt;div class=&quot;blk&quot; id=&quot;mtp-b0&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Block 1&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span&gt;6 layers · ×1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n   &lt;div class=&quot;arr&quot;&gt;→&lt;/div&gt;\n   &lt;div class=&quot;mid&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;tag&quot; id=&quot;mtp-tag&quot;&gt;middle blocks · pass 0 / 3&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;blk&quot; id=&quot;mtp-b1&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Block 2&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span&gt;6 layers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;blk&quot; id=&quot;mtp-b2&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Block 3&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span&gt;6 layers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n   &lt;/div&gt;\n   &lt;div class=&quot;arr&quot;&gt;→&lt;/div&gt;\n   &lt;div class=&quot;blk&quot; id=&quot;mtp-b3&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Block 4&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span&gt;6 layers · ×1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;counter&quot;&gt;layer applications: &lt;big id=&quot;mtp-cnt&quot;&gt;0&lt;/big&gt; / 48&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;meter&quot;&gt;&lt;i id=&quot;mtp-meter&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;msg&quot; id=&quot;mtp-msg&quot;&gt;Press Step to send 1 token through the model.&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;ctrl&quot;&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;btn pri&quot; id=&quot;mtp-step&quot;&gt;Step&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;btn&quot; id=&quot;mtp-play&quot;&gt;Auto-play&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;btn&quot; id=&quot;mtp-reset&quot;&gt;Reset&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;p class=&quot;note&quot;&gt;Middle-block looping gave a 1.51x to 1.91x compute-equivalent gain, vs 1.24x to 1.36x for looping the last layers. It won 27 of 28 evaluations.&lt;/p&gt;\n &lt;/div&gt;\n\n &lt;div class=&quot;panel&quot; id=&quot;p-bm&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;cats&quot;&gt;\n   &lt;button class=&quot;cat on&quot; data-c=&quot;code&quot;&gt;Coding&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;cat&quot; data-c=&quot;agent&quot;&gt;Agentic&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;cat&quot; data-c=&quot;vis&quot;&gt;Vision + docs&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;cat&quot; data-c=&quot;rsn&quot;&gt;Reasoning&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;cat&quot; data-c=&quot;weak&quot;&gt;Weak spots&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div id=&quot;mtp-bars&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;p class=&quot;note&quot;&gt;Black = Inkling 2 Mini (self-reported). Grey = competitor, from its own model card. Red = weakest areas. Harnesses differ across vendors.&lt;/p&gt;\n &lt;/div&gt;\n\n &lt;div class=&quot;panel&quot; id=&quot;p-ef&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;n&quot;&gt;Inkling 2 Mini&lt;small&gt;DGX Spark, MXFP8&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;bar&quot;&gt;&lt;i data-w=&quot;70.3&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;s&quot;&gt;0.703&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;n&quot;&gt;Qwen3.6-35B-A3B&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;bar c&quot;&gt;&lt;i data-w=&quot;43.0&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;s&quot;&gt;0.430&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;n&quot;&gt;Gemma-4-26B-A4B&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;bar c&quot;&gt;&lt;i data-w=&quot;15.9&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;s&quot;&gt;0.159&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;p class=&quot;note&quot;&gt;Stanford Intelligence per Watt scores, as reported by Thinking Machines.&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;two&quot; style=&quot;margin-top:12px&quot;&gt;\n   &lt;div class=&quot;box&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Unlooped baseline&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;7.5% less training compute&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Needed 140% more inference compute to match the looped model's loss on 512k-token agentic traces&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n   &lt;div class=&quot;box&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Training recipe&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;384 experts pruned to 128 at midtraining&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;1T-token distillation heal&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;RL over 2.2T tokens and 2,000 steps&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n &lt;/div&gt;\n\n &lt;div class=&quot;panel&quot; id=&quot;p-run&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;cats mems&quot;&gt;\n   &lt;button class=&quot;cat&quot; data-m=&quot;16&quot;&gt;16GB Mac&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;cat&quot; data-m=&quot;24&quot;&gt;24GB GPU&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;cat&quot; data-m=&quot;32&quot;&gt;32GB Mac&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;cat&quot; data-m=&quot;48&quot;&gt;48GB+ Mac&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;cat&quot; data-m=&quot;spark&quot;&gt;DGX Spark&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;cat&quot; data-m=&quot;gpu32&quot;&gt;32GB+ GPU&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;verdict&quot; id=&quot;mtp-verdict&quot;&gt;Pick your machine to check it against the published requirements.&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;pre&gt;vllm serve &quot;thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Mini&quot;&lt;/pre&gt;\n  &lt;p class=&quot;note&quot;&gt;Also supported: Transformers, SGLang, Ollama, NVIDIA Dynamo, TokenSpeed, llama.cpp (GGUF) and Tinker.&lt;/p&gt;\n &lt;/div&gt;\n\n &lt;div class=&quot;panel&quot; id=&quot;p-tr&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;two&quot;&gt;\n   &lt;div class=&quot;box&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Strengths&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;79.2% SWE-bench Verified (bash only)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;20.1 AA Index, tied with Qwen3.8-27B&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;92.8% OmniDocBench v1.6&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Runs on a 32GB Mac&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n   &lt;div class=&quot;box&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Caveats&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;-8.6 AA-Omniscience, 63.4% non-hallucination rate&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;50.0% MultiChallenge, 33.4% ComplexConstraints&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Can get stuck in long reasoning loops&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Local looped-model runtimes are new, speed varies&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n &lt;/div&gt;\n\n &lt;div class=&quot;ft&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Sources: &lt;a href=&quot;https://thinkingmachines.ai/news/inkling-2-mini/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;blog&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://thinkingmachines.ai/model-card/inkling-2-mini/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;model card&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href=&quot;https://huggingface.co/thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Mini&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;weights&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;brand&quot;&gt;© Marktechpost&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n(function(){\nvar R=document.getElementById('mtp-ink2m');\nfunction resize(){try{parent.postMessage({mtpInk2mHeight:R.offsetHeight+40},'*');}catch(e){}}\nR.querySelectorAll('.tab').forEach(function(t){t.addEventListener('click',function(){\n R.querySelectorAll('.tab').forEach(function(x){x.classList.remove('on')});t.classList.add('on');\n R.querySelectorAll('.panel').forEach(function(p){p.classList.remove('on')});\n var p=document.getElementById('p-'+t.dataset.p);p.classList.add('on');\n if(t.dataset.p==='bm')drawBars(cur);\n if(t.dataset.p==='ef')animate(p);\n setTimeout(resize,60);\n});});\nR.querySelectorAll('.tile').forEach(function(t){t.addEventListener('click',function(){t.classList.toggle('open');setTimeout(resize,320);});});\nfunction animate(scope){scope.querySelectorAll('.bar i').forEach(function(i){i.style.width='0';setTimeout(function(){i.style.width=i.dataset.w+'%'},40);});}\n/* loop stepper */\nvar steps=[{b:[0],c:6,m:'Block 1 runs once: 6 layer applications.'},\n{b:[1,2],c:18,m:'Middle pass 1 of 3: 12 more layers.'},\n{b:[1,2],c:30,m:'Pass 2: same weights, plus a gated &quot;message&quot; from pass 1.'},\n{b:[1,2],c:42,m:'Pass 3: message from pass 2 via Attention Residuals.'},\n{b:[3],c:48,m:'Block 4 runs once. Done: 48 applications from 24 stored layers.'}];\nvar k=-1,timer=null;\nfunction show(){for(var j=0;j&lt;4;j++)document.getElementById('mtp-b'+j).classList.remove('act');\n if(k&lt;0){document.getElementById('mtp-cnt').textContent='0';document.getElementById('mtp-meter').style.width='0';document.getElementById('mtp-msg').textContent='Press Step to send 1 token through the model.';document.getElementById('mtp-tag').textContent='middle blocks · pass 0 / 3';return;}\n var s=steps[k];s.b.forEach(function(j){document.getElementById('mtp-b'+j).classList.add('act')});\n document.getElementById('mtp-cnt').textContent=s.c;document.getElementById('mtp-meter').style.width=(s.c/48*100)+'%';\n document.getElementById('mtp-msg').textContent=s.m;\n var pass=k===0?0:(k&gt;=1&amp;&amp;k&lt;=3?k:3);document.getElementById('mtp-tag').textContent='middle blocks · pass '+pass+' / 3';}\nfunction step(){k=(k+1)%steps.length;show();}\ndocument.getElementById('mtp-step').onclick=function(){if(timer){clearInterval(timer);timer=null;}step();};\ndocument.getElementById('mtp-reset').onclick=function(){if(timer){clearInterval(timer);timer=null;}k=-1;show();};\ndocument.getElementById('mtp-play').onclick=function(){if(timer){clearInterval(timer);timer=null;return;}k=-1;show();timer=setInterval(function(){step();if(k===steps.length-1){clearInterval(timer);timer=null;}},1100);};\n/* benchmarks */\nvar D={code:[['SWE-bench Verified','bash only',79.2,''],['SWE-bench Pro v2 (Hard)','',77.9,''],['DeepSWE v1.1','Inkling 2 Mini',48.2,''],['DeepSWE v1.1','Qwen3.8-27B',42.2,'c'],['Terminal Bench v2.1','Inkling 2 Mini',71.6,''],['Terminal Bench v2.1','Qwen3.8-27B',73.0,'c']],\nagent:[['BrowseComp','with compaction',79.0,''],['MCP Atlas','public',82.7,'']],\nvis:[['OmniDocBench v1.6','',92.8,''],['MMMU Pro','Standard 10',74.9,'']],\nrsn:[['GPQA Diamond','Inkling 2 Mini',86.6,''],['GPQA Diamond','Qwen3.8-27B',89.2,'c'],['GPQA Diamond','Qwen3.6-35B-A3B',86.0,'c'],['GPQA Diamond','Gemma 4 26B A4B',82.3,'c'],['ARC-AGI-2','',49.3,'']],\nweak:[['HLE-Diamond','',15.2,'w'],['ComplexConstraints v1.1','',33.4,'w'],['MultiChallenge','',50.0,'w'],['AA-Omniscience','non-hallucination rate',63.4,'w']]};\nvar cur='code';\nfunction drawBars(c){cur=c;var h='';D[c].forEach(function(r){h+='&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;n&quot;&gt;'+r[0]+(r[1]?'&lt;small&gt;'+r[1]+'&lt;/small&gt;':'')+'&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;bar '+r[3]+'&quot;&gt;&lt;i data-w=&quot;'+r[2]+'&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;s&quot;&gt;'+r[2].toFixed(1)+'%&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;';});\n var el=document.getElementById('mtp-bars');el.innerHTML=h;animate(el);setTimeout(resize,60);}\nR.querySelectorAll('.cat[data-c]').forEach(function(b){b.addEventListener('click',function(){R.querySelectorAll('.cat[data-c]').forEach(function(x){x.classList.remove('on')});b.classList.add('on');drawBars(b.dataset.c);});});\n/* run checker */\nvar V={'16':['no','Below the published minimum.','Thinking Machines lists Apple silicon with 32GB or more. No smaller official requirement is published.'],\n'24':['no','Below the recommended VRAM.','The model card recommends GPUs with 32GB or more of VRAM. Unsloth and llama.cpp offer quantized GGUF builds, but no 24GB requirement is published.'],\n'32':['ok','Supported.','Apple silicon with 32GB or more is a listed setup, via Ollama or Exo Labs.'],\n'48':['ok','Supported.','Thinking Machines built its PlaneBench demo offline on a MacBook Pro (M5 Pro, 48GB).'],\n'spark':['ok','Supported, with native NVFP4.','1 NVIDIA DGX Spark is a listed setup. The 0.703 Intelligence per Watt score was measured here.'],\n'gpu32':['ok','Recommended.','Other GPUs with 32GB or more of VRAM are recommended. Serve with vLLM, SGLang or Transformers.']};\nR.querySelectorAll('.cat[data-m]').forEach(function(b){b.addEventListener('click',function(){R.querySelectorAll('.cat[data-m]').forEach(function(x){x.classList.remove('on')});b.classList.add('on');var v=V[b.dataset.m];document.getElementById('mtp-verdict').innerHTML='&lt;b class=&quot;'+v[0]+'&quot;&gt;'+v[1]+'&lt;/b&gt; '+v[2];setTimeout(resize,60);});});\nwindow.addEventListener('load',resize);window.addEventListener('resize',resize);setTimeout(resize,300);\n})();\n&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;\n\"></iframe>\n  </div>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-how-does-inkling-2-mini-compare-with-qwen-and-gemma\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How does Inkling 2 Mini compare with Qwen and Gemma?</strong></h2>\n  <figure class=\"wp-block-table\">\n   <table class=\"has-fixed-layout\">\n    <thead>\n     <tr>\n      <th>Feature</th>\n      <th><strong>Inkling 2 Mini</strong> (<a href=\"https://thinkingmachines.ai/model-card/inkling-2-mini/\">card</a>)</th>\n      <th>Qwen3.8-27B (<a href=\"https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B\">card</a>)</th>\n      <th>Qwen3.6-35B-A3B (<a href=\"https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B\">card</a>)</th>\n      <th>Gemma 4 26B A4B (<a href=\"https://ai.google.dev/gemma/docs/core/model_card_4\">card</a>)</th>\n     </tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n     <tr>\n      <td>Architecture</td>\n      <td>Looped MoE</td>\n      <td>Dense</td>\n      <td>MoE</td>\n      <td>MoE</td>\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n      <td>Total params</td>\n      <td>26.4B</td>\n      <td>27B</td>\n      <td>35B</td>\n      <td>25.2B</td>\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n      <td>Active params</td>\n      <td>3.4B (5.4B effective)</td>\n      <td>27B (dense)</td>\n      <td>3B</td>\n      <td>3.8B</td>\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n      <td>Context</td>\n      <td>Up to 1M</td>\n      <td>262,144 native, up to 1M</td>\n      <td>262,144 native, up to 1,010,000</td>\n      <td>256K</td>\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n      <td>License</td>\n      <td>Apache 2.0</td>\n      <td>Apache 2.0</td>\n      <td>Apache 2.0</td>\n      <td>Apache 2.0</td>\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n      <td>Input</td>\n      <td>Text, image</td>\n      <td>Text, image, video</td>\n      <td>Text, image</td>\n      <td>Text, image</td>\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n      <td>Hardware listed</td>\n      <td>~20GB; 32GB Mac or DGX Spark</td>\n      <td>Not disclosed</td>\n      <td>Not disclosed</td>\n      <td>Not disclosed</td>\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n      <td>GPQA Diamond</td>\n      <td>86.6%</td>\n      <td>89.2</td>\n      <td>86.0</td>\n      <td>82.3%</td>\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n      <td>Terminal Bench 2.1</td>\n      <td>71.6%</td>\n      <td>73.0</td>\n      <td>Not reported</td>\n      <td>Not reported</td>\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n      <td>SWE-bench Verified</td>\n      <td>79.2% (bash only)</td>\n      <td>Not reported</td>\n      <td>73.4</td>\n      <td>Not reported</td>\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n      <td>DeepSWE 1.1</td>\n      <td>48.2%</td>\n      <td>42.2</td>\n      <td>Not reported</td>\n      <td>Not reported</td>\n     </tr>\n     <tr>\n      <td>Hosted access</td>\n      <td>Tinker</td>\n      <td>Qwen Cloud</td>\n      <td>Not disclosed</td>\n      <td>Not disclosed</td>\n     </tr>\n    </tbody>\n   </table>\n  </figure>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Each column uses the vendor’s own model card. Harnesses and settings differ, so treat cross-vendor gaps as directional.</em></p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-what-hardware-do-you-need-to-run-inkling-2-mini\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>What hardware do you need to run Inkling 2 Mini?</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The checkpoint is about 20GB in Safetensors. Thinking Machines lists 3 supported setups: 1 NVIDIA DGX Spark, Apple silicon with 32GB+ memory, and other GPUs with 32GB+ VRAM. Quantized GGUF builds are available through Unsloth and llama.cpp.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Serving support covers Transformers, vLLM, SGLang, Ollama, NVIDIA Dynamo and TokenSpeed. Tinker pricing for Mini is not disclosed in the launch materials.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A vLLM quick start takes 1 command: <code>vllm serve \"thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Mini\"</code>.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-where-does-inkling-2-mini-fall-short\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Where does Inkling 2 Mini fall short?</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Knowledge depends mostly on total parameters, and looping did not help knowledge benchmarks. Inkling 2 Mini scores -8.6 on AA-Omniscience, with a 63.4% non-hallucination rate.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It is not the best small model for multi-turn chat or constraint-heavy prompts. It scores 50.0% on MultiChallenge and 33.4% on ComplexConstraints v1.1. It also trails larger models on HLE-Diamond (15.2%) and CritPt v2.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-key-takeaways\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Key Takeaways</strong></h2>\n  <ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n   <li>Inkling 2 Mini loops 24 stored layers into 48 layer passes per token.</li>\n   <li>26.4B total, 3.4B active, ~20GB, Apache 2.0, up to 1M context.</li>\n   <li>Runs on a 32GB Mac or 1 DGX Spark via Ollama, vLLM or llama.cpp.</li>\n   <li>Scores 79.2% on SWE-bench Verified and ties Qwen3.8-27B at 20.1 AA Index.</li>\n   <li>Weak spots: knowledge recall, multi-turn chat and constraint-heavy prompts.</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n  <hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Check out the <a href=\"https://thinkingmachines.ai/news/inkling-2-mini/\"><strong>technical blog</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://thinkingmachines.ai/model-card/inkling-2-mini/\"><strong>model card</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Mini\"><strong>model weights</strong></a> and<strong> <a href=\"https://tinker.thinkingmachines.ai/playground\">Tinker Playground</a></strong>. You can check the deployment options and specs here through our <strong><a href=\"https://aicampaign.live/gpu-1\">GPULeaderboard.com chrome extension</a></strong>.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Also,&nbsp;feel free to follow us on&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://x.com/intent/follow?screen_name=marktechpost\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><mark>Twitter</mark></a></strong>&nbsp;and don’t forget to join our&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/machinelearningnews/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">150k+ML SubReddit</a></strong>&nbsp;and Subscribe to&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/2026/11/08/google-elephant-goldfish-model-plugin-spec-review-coding-agents/#aids-signup\">our Newsletter</a></strong>. Wait! are you on telegram?&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://t.me/machinelearningresearchnews\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">now you can join us on telegram as well.</a></strong></p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Need to partner with us for promoting your GitHub Repo OR Hugging Face Page OR Product Release OR Webinar etc.?&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://promotions.marktechpost.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><mark>Connect with us</mark></a></strong></p>\n  <!-- MOLONGUI AUTHORSHIP PLUGIN 5.3.2 -->\n  